The root cause is name collision: Apex identifiers are case-insensitive, so a loop variable named `lead` shadows the `Lead` sObject, and `Lead.Email` then resolves as a dynamic property on the variable (its String value) instead of the static field token. Fixed by using loop variable `rec` and the standard static field references.

